WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.650
1. Squeeze the front brake and watch the pads meet the rim

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:20.250
2. Turn the bike over, open the quick release and drop the wheel out

00:00:20.250 --> 00:01:13.950
3. Take the skewer out: nut off, slide it out, springs narrow end in

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:31.650
4. Spin the wheel and run your fingers round the braking track

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:40.350
5. Check the brake calipers and pads from above

00:01:40.350 --> 00:02:05.050
6. Set the wheel back in the fork with the tread arrow pointing forward, then check the rear tire the same way

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:35.750
7. Slide the skewer back through the hub and thread the nut on

00:02:35.750 --> 00:03:02.550
8. Snug the nut and close the lever flat along the fork

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:20.066
9. Turn the bike upright, spin the wheel and squeeze the brake

